From 04b715a7ac0e5232d49fc6fbb4f4465a43b13679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:15:08 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] [Video] Don't look for a disc in a plugin folder queued from
 the library

With "Play next video automatically" on, playing an episode from the
library queues its season, and since #29871 LoadDetails() gives the
season item its folder as the dynamic path. In a library whose files
are plugin:// paths, as the Jellyfin add-on writes them, that folder is
a plugin path, and the check for a DVD or Blu-ray folder finds one
there because CPluginFile::Exists() is true for any path. The season is
then queued as <folder>/VIDEO_TS.IFO, which the plugin can't resolve,
and nothing plays.

Skip that check when the dynamic path is a plugin path too, as it is
already skipped for plugin folders.

Assisted-by: Claude
(cherry picked from commit 2987158156a63e78a70f8060cea39508ca6ccde5)
---
 xbmc/video/guilib/VideoGUIUtils.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/video/guilib/VideoGUIUtils.cpp b/xbmc/video/guilib/VideoGUIUtils.cpp
index 8598b81..68daef8 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/guilib/VideoGUIUtils.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/guilib/VideoGUIUtils.cpp
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@ void CAsyncGetItemsForPlaylist::GetItemsForPlaylist(const std::shared_ptr<CFileI
 
   if (item->IsFolder())
   {
-    if (!item->IsPlugin())
+    if (!item->IsPlugin() && !item->GetDynURL().IsPlugin())
     {
       // check if it's a folder with dvd or bluray files, then just add the relevant file
       const std::string mediapath = VIDEO::UTILS::GetOpticalMediaPath(*item);
